{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547464-would-an-amphiptere-make-a-good-mage-familiar","id":1547464,"title":"Would an Amphiptere make a good mage familiar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-02T13:54:03-08:00","id":1547464,"title":"Would an Amphiptere make a good mage familiar?","content":"Considering that they can naturally eat paradox would they make great familiars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T15:10:32-08:00","id":1547465,"title":"","content":"I suppose a mage could have a familiar which takes that form, or attempt to find a Bygone amphiptere and form some sort of companion relationship with one, though the latter would be a consor rather than a familiar. In either case you'd want to provide a suitable environment for it, just as with any other sort of familiar or exotic consor. Depending on where a mage lives, this might be a bit challenging. Familiars <i>are </i>intelligent NPCs, and maintaining a good relationship with one does require more than weekly feedings of quintessence.<br /> <br /> Any sort of familiar can absorb Paradox from their mage, though they <i>don't </i>like doing this as it's not at all a pleasant experience for them. Only a couple of the mage characters in the games I run have had familiars, and I don't recall either of them ever asking their familiar to do this, though it's happened a couple times that a familiar has done it without being asked in a dire emergency. One character is highly protective of her feline familiar best friend, pampers him endlessly, and would be horrified by the mere suggestion of feeding him Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T15:43:29-08:00","id":1547467,"title":"","content":"Well, considering they can take human-shape and they like mages they can work as a pretty convenient familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T17:08:54-08:00","id":1547468,"title":"","content":"Maybe if they had the addition of elemental touch they could control air to an extent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T18:29:43-08:00","id":1547470,"title":"","content":"They could have the demeanor of a fleeting dilettante and the nature of a gentle friend. She's interested in the magical arts and grew up in Horizon until it got destroyed by The Avatar Storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 01-02-2025, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T19:49:37-08:00","id":1547471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547464-would-an-amphiptere-make-a-good-mage-familiar?p=1547470#post1547470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have the demeanor of a fleeting dilettante and the nature of a gentle friend. She's interested in the magical arts and grew up in Horizon until it got destroyed by The Avatar Storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>If she was born and raised in Horizon, she'd most likely have more familiarity with exotic familiars and consors than the average mage. The few times characters have visited Horizon in the games I've run, both I and the players had fun playing up some of the culture shock even very experienced mages not familiar with the environment and society would inevitably deal with. It's one thing to understand and use magick, it's quite another to have spent most of your life talking about it only behind closed doors and mainly working only subtle effects, only to suddenly be plunged into a setting where such things are spoken of very openly and publicly, and comparatively vulgar effects are commonplace without natives usually batting an eye.<br /> <br /> Part of the charm of familiars is that they're beings which are somewhat mysterious, even to the mages who pact with them. They can tend to have a somewhat alien view of the world at times, some more than others, and even those who're <i>very</i> happy to live as pampered cats have complex ideas and motivations of their own (which are not always overtly expressed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}